which Cameo and Doctor Strange in the  Multiverse of Madness will leave fans  who aren't Comics readers scratching  their heads and which one will make Sam  Raimi fans scream with delight keep  watching for our ranking from worst to  best as you might suspect it's all  spoilers from here  in the mid-credits scene of Doctor  Strange in the Multiverse of Madness Dr  Strange is greeted on the street by a  woman in purple with long blonde hair  insisting he go with her to fix a new  multiversal incursion this character  played by Charlize Theron gets no real  introduction which is sure to confuse a  lot of viewers not familiar with the  doctor strange Comics the credits  confirm that Theron's character is Clea  who hails from the dark dimension and is  nice of dormammu given the character's  romantic history with Dr Strange there's  certainly plenty of potential for CLIA  to be a great character in future movies  and the idea of Theron joining the MCU  might be enough of a tease for viewers  who don't read Comics but that doesn't  make the Cameo itself any more coherent  rintra is a green Minotaur and one of  the sorcerers at kamartaj while he may  be more of a minor supporting character  than a cameo exactly his presence is odd  enough to elicit the same sort of who is  that response since renshra receives no  proper introductions some viewers might  wonder if they forgot him from the first  Doctor Strange movie but neither he nor  any member of his alien species have  appeared in the MCU before now he's just  there because Marvel had the extra  effects budget for a CGI Minotaur it  seems in a way it's kind of impressive  that Marvel Studios has made audiences  so accustomed to comic book weirdness  that a giant green Minotaur alien can  show up without even being remarked upon  the robots at the Illuminati  headquarters don't look exactly like the  Ultron MCU fans are familiar with but  one of them can be heard making commands  in the name of Ultron when Scarlet Witch  first makes her attack the credits  confirm these robots are indeed meant to  be alternate universe versions of Ultron  played by the characters what if voice  actor Ross Marquand there are worlds  beyond my own worlds that needs me the  alternate ultron's presence does present  some interesting World building for this  alternate universe clearly they didn't  try to kill all humans like the one in  Age of Ultron so one has to wonder how  they came to be were they created by  Tony Stark like on Earth 616 perhaps  they were a project of Reed Richards and  the Baxter Foundation or maybe they're a  Hank Pym creation like in the original  comics  on Earth 616 Maria Rambo was Carol  danver's best friend on Earth One  Division revealed she died of cancer  during the blip so it's nice to see her  again as the Captain Marvel of the  Illuminati Universe like all the members  of the Illuminati she's killed by  Scarlet Witch fairly easily and her  death is perhaps the most frustrating of  the bunch director Sam raimi's  willingness to risk fan anger by killing  off characters is one of the strong  points of Multiverse of Madness but the  way Rambo's death is handled is pretty  weak Captain Marvel is supposed to be  one of the strongest superheroes around  yet this version of her is simply  dispatched by a falling statue surely  there could have been a more intense and  scary death scene that didn't minimize  her power  what if built up Captain Carter a Peggy  Carter variant who took the super  soldier serum instead of Steve Rogers to  be a key character given the appearances  of her shield and trailers it's not  particularly surprising but still really  cool to see Haley Atwell get a chance to  play Captain Carter in live action in  Multiverse of Madness like the other  Illuminati members Captain Carter's  screen time is fairly brief but it's  structured effectively with a fun action  scene paralleling Rogers famous I'm  gonna do this all day moment she's  killed in the most brutal and ironic way  possible by her own Shield  these short-lived Inhumans TV show was a  pretty Infamous flop so seeing Anson  mount's Black Bolt show up as part of  the Illuminati comes as a surprise  Bolt's emergence from a rare MCU misstep  might be why strange seems to Target him  with his sardonic humor his death also  makes him seem not too bright black  Bolt's words can kill in a flashback to  the Illuminati dispatching their  universe as Doctor Strange it's his I'm  sorry that finishes him off this power  is turned against him by Scarlet witch  who cleverly removes his mouth just as  he is about to speak the sound gets  locked inside his skull which explodes  from the inside  casting John Krasinski as Mr Fantastic  and Multiverse of Madness is either the  ultimate fan service or the ultimate  troll there's no official word of who  will play Reed Richards in the  forthcoming Fantastic Four MCU entry but  casting Krasinski here matches up with  some of the most popular fan casts this  version of Mr Fantastic doesn't last  long he's the second Illuminati member  killed by Scarlet Witch when she  essentially shreds his body into string  cheese if Krasinski indeed returns as  the Reed of Earth 616 this could be an  unorthodox introduction to one of the  next great MCU Heroes like John Travolta  and Pulp Fiction audiences will have  watched him die well before his story is  over  rather than reprising the Incarnation of  the character he played in the fox X-Men  films Patrick Stewart seems to be  playing the version of Professor X from  the 90s X-Men animated series given the  design of his chair and the music that  plays during his introduction  Stuart as Xavier is a perfect bit of fan  service which will appeal to multiple  generations of Marvel fans the  characters psychic powers make him  seemingly the ideal match to face the  mental manipulations of the Scarlet  Witch if any of the Illuminati could win  the battle against her it would have  been him which makes his death all the  more intense and upsetting  for all the Marvel fan service scattered  throughout Multiverse of Madness the  best thing about the movie is just how  strongly director Sam raimi's  sensibility shines throughout there's  wild cinematography wacky fun house  horror and of course a cameo from Bruce  Campbell Campbell made his big break as  Ash Williams the hero of raymie's Evil  Dead series and the actor continues to  play ridiculous Parts in the director's  other films his part in Multiverse of  Madness is a parallel universe Pizza  ball salesman named Pizza Papa whom Dr  Strange afflicts with a curse that  forces him to beat himself up in a clear  Evil Dead reference the film's  post-credits scene catches up with pizza  Papa as the curse finally wears off a  funny bit that's also strangely  satisfying  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more Looper videos about  the MCU are coming soon subscribe to our  YouTube channel and hit the Bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

